## Summary

Per the public archive of Lauren Tan's posts: a recent pstack release
introduces `/create-formal-verification-skill`, a skill that generates
verification workflows for coding agents using formal methods — TLA+ for
state machines, Kani (Rust model checking) for bounded code properties.

## Provenance note

Evidence is second-hand: the claim is read from a public X archive mirror,
not from pstack's release notes directly. The repo reference needs to be
confirmed (candidate: github.com/poteto/pstack) before promotion.

## ATL recommendation

P0: ATL already models the task lifecycle (verification/atl_manager_lifecycle_model.py).
Extend that discipline to the queue: explicit invariants for queue state,
agent ownership, retries, concurrency (run lease), and crash recovery —
generated and checked the way pstack does, so runtime waves cannot silently
violate them.
